@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Candidate web middleware chain — owner checks remain essential
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Request / trusted transport boundary" as I
rectangle "Bounded correlation context\nTreat incoming metadata as untrusted" as C
rectangle "Payload/media limits / schema boundary" as V
rectangle "Applicable session/authentication / anti-forgery controls" as S
rectangle "Reviewed abuse / resource admission" as R
rectangle "Resource-owning handler\nCurrent scoped authorization + lifecycle/version invariant" as H
rectangle "Permitted result / error projection\nRestricted diagnostic hooks" as O
I --> C
C --> V
V --> S
S --> R
R --> H
H --> O
legend bottom
 Illustrative responsibilities/order; actual framework routes and early-return/error paths need evaluation.
 A global authenticated middleware cannot replace per-resource authorization or protect bypass routes by assertion.
 Jobs/native clients/callbacks need equivalent applicable checks, not necessarily this HTTP chain.
endlegend
@enduml
